title: The Emissaries
subtitle: Béla Kun arrives from Moscow with a theory.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1921 and month = 3 and e21_kun_done = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 10
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_kun_done = 1;
Q.e21_lux_leads = (Q.leading_faction == 'luxemburgist') ? 1 : 0;
Q.comintern_rep = 'Béla Kun';
if (Q.comintern_member == 1) {
    RG.directive({
        id: 'offensive',
        title: 'The theory of the offensive',
        text: 'The revolutionary party does not wait to be attacked. The Executive instructs the German section to go over to the offensive at the first occasion, to rouse the masses by action, and if necessary to force the pace.',
        from: 'zinoviev',
        months: 2,
        goals: [{q: 'militancy', op: '>=', v: Math.min(85, Math.round(Q.militancy + 10))},
                {q: 'red_guards_arms', op: '>=', v: Math.min(85, Math.round(Q.red_guards_arms + 8))}],
        reward: {subsidy: 1, faction: 'offensive'},
        punish: 'rival',
        announce: false
    });
}
!}

= The Emissaries

In the first days of March three men arrive from Moscow: Béla Kun, who led the Hungarian soviet republic to its fall in 1919, József Pogány and August Guralsky. They come from Zinoviev. Soviet Russia is isolated, Kronstadt is in revolt, and the German party must go over to the offensive: act, and if necessary provoke, until the masses move.

[? if e21_levi_resigned = 1 : Kun goes to see Levi and Zetkin out of courtesy. Zetkin tells him his plan is madness, and Levi writes to Lenin. ?][? if e21_levi_resigned = 0 and levi_in_party = 1 : Kun goes first to Levi, who still holds the chair. Levi listens for an hour and shows him to the door. ?] Thalheimer and Frölich are already writing in the Rote Fahne that a revolutionary party cannot wait to be attacked.

- @embrace: Adopt the theory of the offensive.
- @prepare: Prepare to defend the party, not to attack.
- @refuse: Send Kun back to Moscow.
- @arm: Arm the councils in every city at once.

@embrace
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The districts will be told to look for a pretext. Zinoviev and Bukharin will be pleased.
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids taking orders from Moscow.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e21_offensive_plan = 3;
Q.militancy += 8;
Q.lean_offensive += 3;
RG.comply(40);
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 6);
RG.ecci('bukharin', 8);
RG.ledger('The Zentrale adopted the theory of the offensive.', 'e21_offensive_adopted');
!}

The Zentrale accepts Kun's line. The districts are told to be ready for action at any moment, and to look for an occasion. Nobody says out loud what kind.

@prepare
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. Strike committees and courier lines in Central Germany, for the fight everyone expects. Radek will approve.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no money to prepare anything.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.e21_offensive_plan = 2;
RG.district('halle', {guards: 1});
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
RG.comply(15);
RG.ecci('radek', 5);
!}

Kun is thanked for his advice and given an office. Meanwhile the Zentrale sets up strike committees, courier lines and arms caches in Central Germany, ready for when the enemy strikes first.

@refuse
subtitle: The German party will decide when it fights. Moscow's money will be shorter.
choose-if: e21_lux_leads = 1
unavailable-subtitle: Without Levi at its head, nobody in the Zentrale will defy Moscow's envoys.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_offensive_plan = 1;
Q.moscow_subsidy = Math.max(0, Q.moscow_subsidy - 1);
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 3;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -6);
RG.ecci('lenin', 3);
RG.defy();
!}

The Zentrale tells Kun that the German party will decide for itself when and how to fight. Kun stays in Berlin anyway, and spends his evenings with Ruth Fischer.

@arm
view-if: ultraleft_gone = 0
subtitle: Hamburg and Bremen want more than Kun does. Lenin will be appalled.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e21_offensive_plan = 3;
Q.lean_ultraleft += 3;
RG.district('hamburg', {militancy: 8, guards: 0.5});
RG.district('bremen', {militancy: 8});
RG.ecci('lenin', -8);
!}

Hamburg and Bremen send their own men to the Mansfeld pits with rifles. Kun is delighted. The Zentrale is no longer sure who is leading whom.
